This library is an independent, from-scratch Python reimplementation.
No source code was copied from the projects below; behavior and file-
format semantics were derived from reading their sources and are
attributed here:

* OpenCMISS-Zinc (cmlibs-zinc), Auckland Bioengineering Institute,
  University of Auckland — Mozilla Public License 2.0.
  The EX/EXF reader and writer mirror the productions of Zinc's
  import_finite_element.cpp / export_finite_element.cpp so the two
  implementations can be reviewed side by side; basis function
  ordering follows finite_element_basis.cpp; face-inheritance maps
  follow finite_element_shape.cpp; coordinate-system conversion
  formulas follow general/geometry.cpp. exfield's numerical results
  are golden-validated against Zinc 4.2.1.

* VTK (The Visualization Toolkit), Kitware, Inc. — BSD-3-Clause.
  The higher-order cell point ordering in exfield/vtu.py is a
  transcription of vtkHigherOrderCurve/Quadrilateral/Hexahedron
  ::PointIndexFromIJK, pinned against tables generated by VTK 9.6.2.

Test data (tests/data/, not part of the installed package):

* sub-f001_L_vagus_scaffold.exf and golden_f001_L.json derive from
  SPARC dataset 426 (pennsieve.io / sparc.science; SPARC datasets are
  published under CC-BY-4.0 — see the dataset page for citation).
* cube.exf is vendored from the sparc.client project's test fixtures.
